{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ERA5",
    "description": "ERA5 regridding model — the coupler half of the era5 loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.1). Exposes ERA5 ECMWF Reanalysis 5th Generation pressure-level fields on the simulation's target grid for coupling into EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6):\n  1. It declares the pure-I/O source inline: at 0.7.0 the loader was the separate file components/earthsci_data/era5_loader.esm, mounted as the subsystem `pl`; at esm 1.0.0 it is the `ERA5_pl` entry in this file's own `data_sources` and the standalone file is gone (a data source is not a component, so it neither needs nor may be a subsystem). Loader fields are referenced as ERA5.pl.<var> (e.g. ERA5.pl.u).\n  2. Reprojection & regridding are NOT model concerns at esm 0.8.0. ERA5's native grid is geographic (longlat/WGS84); the identity longlat reprojection and the per-variable regridding onto a consuming grid (conservative for centered scalars t/q/r/z/w/…, B-spline for the horizontal winds u/v) are expressed at the COUPLING EDGE as coupling expressions (esm-spec §8.6/§10.5) by importing the earthscidiscretizations reprojection/ and regridding/ template libraries — see the wildlandfire.esm assembler. This model no longer carries a `regrid` block.\n\nTop-level derived quantities computed on the target grid: pressure P (from the 37-entry pressure-level lookup table), and the lat/lon coordinate metrics δxδlon and δyδlat (emitted only for lat/lon coordinate domains).\n\nMeanWind coupling (from EarthSciData.jl@830435a coupling.jl): MeanWind.v_lon ~ ERA5.pl.u, MeanWind.v_lat ~ ERA5.pl.v, MeanWind.v_lev ~ ERA5.pl.w.\n\nMigration esm 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0 (this file): v0.8.0 is a clean break that REMOVED `Model.regrid`/`RegridSpec` (esm-spec §8.6). Accordingly the former model `regrid` block (per-variable conservative/bspline methods) has been REMOVED and the regridding is now performed at the coupling edge via imported template libraries. The loader fields are consumed directly as ERA5.pl.<var>.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385 (ERA5 constructor, esm-te2e); split into pure loader + regridding model by esm-3nc.1.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "reanalysis",
      "era5",
      "ecmwf",
      "pressure_levels",
      "global",
      "regridding_model",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
