      "description": "ERA5 pressure levels in Pa (= hPa * 100). Index 1 = 1000 hPa (near-surface), index 37 = 1 hPa (top of atmosphere). ERA5_PRESSURE_LEVELS_HPA = [1000, 975, 950, 925, 900, 875, 850, 825, 800, 775, 750, 700, 650, 600, 550, 500, 450, 400, 350, 300, 250, 225, 200, 175, 150, 125, 100, 70, 50, 30, 20, 10, 7, 5, 3, 2, 1] converted to Pa. Used by the observed variable P (table_lookup with lev input), reproducing the upstream era5_P_itp LinearInterpolation of levels 1:37 → hPa values."
