          "valid_time"
        ],
        "file_naming": "era5_pl_{YYYY}_{MM:02d}.nc (monthly, one file per calendar month, all 16 pressure-level variables plus pressure_level dimension)",
        "level_indexing_note": "This loader's pressure_level dimension uses hPa values (1–1000 hPa) matching the NetCDF 'pressure_level' dimension. The regridding model's lev parameter uses 1-based integer indexing (1=1000 hPa, 37=1 hPa) matching the upstream ERA5FileSet convention; the runtime converts lev → hPa using the pressure_levels_hpa table before querying this loader.",
        "access_note": "ERA5 data is available from the Copernicus Climate Data Store (CDS) at https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/. The url_template above uses a placeholder earthsci.dev mirror; in production, set EARTHSCIDATADIR to a local cache directory populated via the CDS API or the EarthSciData.jl ERA5FileSet download utilities.",
        "cds": {
          "dataset": "reanalysis-era5-pressure-levels",
          "format": "netcdf",
          "pressure_levels": [
            1000
          ],
          "description": "Opt-in CDS request descriptor (gap G7). When the loader seam is routed through the EarthSciIO provider adapter (earthsci_ast.data_loaders.esio_provider.esio_provider_factory), this block makes the loader resolve to the real Copernicus CDS API instead of the placeholder earthsci.dev mirror: the adapter builds a per-month `cds://reanalysis-era5-pressure-levels?<request>` URL (earthsciio.era5.era5_cds_url) whose `area` is the simulation domain's WGS84 bounding box, whose `variable` list maps this loader's NetCDF short names (t, u, v, r, …) to the CDS long names, and whose `pressure_level` set is `pressure_levels` below (default: all 37 ERA5 levels). EarthSciIO's registered `cds` transport then submits/polls/downloads the NetCDF asset, authenticating with the PRIVATE-TOKEN from ~/.cdsapirc or $CDSAPI_KEY. The submit→poll→download handshake cannot be expressed as the default ESS opener/fetcher's single HTTP GET, which is why the CDS path lives in the esio adapter rather than the default provider.",
          "pressure_levels_note": "The `pressure_levels` key (a list of hPa integers) trims the CDS request to the levels actually needed; omit it to request the full 37-level set (a large download that exceeds the CDS per-request cost limit when combined with a full month × 24 h × 16 variables). It is set to [1000] here because the consuming wildfire model reduces ERA5 to the ground surface (camp_fire's ground_surface interface, lev=min = 1000 hPa), so only the near-surface level is needed; raise it to the full set for a model that uses the vertical column."
        },
        "temporal_note": "ERA5 monthly files are released with a ~2-month lag. The temporal.end above is approximate; update as new months are released. ERA5 Back Extension covers 1940–1978 with slightly reduced quality; the main ERA5 record begins January 1979.",
        "merged_from": "components/earthsci_data/era5_loader.esm",
        "merge_note": "Merged from the standalone pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/era5_loader.esm, which is deleted by the same commit. The 0.x `X.esm` + `X_loader.esm` split existed only because a loader was a COMPONENT and a {\"ref\"} target had to contain exactly one component. At esm 1.0.0 a data source is NOT a component, not a coupling endpoint and not a scoped-name path root, and `data_sources` no longer counts toward a file's top-level system count — so one file may hold a model AND the data_sources that model consumes and still be mountable by {\"ref\"}. This registry entry is byte-identical to the one the deleted file declared (it was already mirrored here so this document would validate), and the deleted file's own top-level metadata — name, description, tags, created, authors, references — is preserved verbatim in `merged_file_metadata` so no provenance, citation or migration note is lost.",
        "merged_file_metadata": {
          "name": "ERA5_pl_loader",
          "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for ERA5 ECMWF Reanalysis 5th Generation pressure-level fields. Provides hourly pressure-level atmospheric variables (wind, temperature, humidity, geopotential, cloud, ozone, and derived fields) on the native 0.25°×0.25° global longitude/latitude grid, 1940–present, sourced from monthly NetCDF files.\n\nThis is the loader half of the era5 loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.1). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), and its temporal cadence. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/era5.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./era5_loader.esm\"}.\n\nBecause a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence for its variables (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers hourly. (A consumer that needs a single time slice as a static field — e.g. the wildlandfire.esm surface-met coupling — binds one resolved hour as a CONST provider.)\n\nMigration esm 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0 (this file): v0.8.0 is a clean break that REMOVED the DataLoader `grid`/`mesh` descriptor (esm-spec §8.4; esm-schema.json DataLoader is now additionalProperties:false over {kind, source, temporal, determinism, variables, reference, metadata} with no `grid` key). Accordingly the former GDD `grid` block (family/crs/dimensions/extents + the n_pressure_level parameter) has been REMOVED. Grid geometry is now ordinary data: the native 0.25°×0.25° lon/lat lattice and the 37 pressure levels are documented in metadata below and materialized downstream by `aggregate` FAQs / coupling expressions (esm-spec §8.6). Reprojection (longlat identity) and conservative/bspline regridding onto a consuming grid are performed at the coupling edge via the reprojection/ and regridding/ template libraries in earthscidiscretizations, NOT here.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385 (ERA5FileSet, pressure-level variables). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/era5.esm (esm-te2e); grid block removed in the 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0 migration.",
          "tags": [
            "earthsci_data",
            "meteorology",
            "reanalysis",
            "era5",
            "ecmwf",
            "pressure_levels",
            "global",
            "data_loader",
            "pure-io",
            "longlat"
          ],
          "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
          "authors": [
            "ECMWF",
            "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.1)"
          ],
          "references": [
            {
              "citation": "Hersbach, H., Bell, B., Berrisford, P., Hirahara, S., Horanyi, A., Munoz-Sabater, J., Nicolas, J., Peubey, C., Radu, R., Schepers, D., Simmons, A., Soci, C., Abdalla, S., Abellan, X., Balsamo, G., Bechtold, P., Biavati, G., Bidlot, J., Bonavita, M., De Chiara, G., Dahlgren, P., Dee, D., Diamantakis, M., Dragani, R., Flemming, J., Forbes, R., Fuentes, M., Geer, A., Haimberger, L., Healy, S., Hogan, R. J., Holm, E., Janiskova, M., Keeley, S., Laloyaux, P., Lopez, P., Lupu, C., Radnoti, G., de Rosnay, P., Rozum, I., Vamborg, F., Villaume, S., and Thepaut, J.-N. (2020). The ERA5 global reanalysis. Quarterly Journal of the Royal Meteorological Society, 146(730), 1999–2049.",
              "url": "https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/dataset/ecmwf-reanalysis-v5",
              "doi": "10.1002/qj.3803"
            },
            {
              "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385 (ERA5 constructor). ERA5FileSet, ERA5_PRESSURE_LEVELS_HPA."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "ERA5": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/era5.jl:385\n\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.1). The pre-migration era5.esm carried both the coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.ERA5_pl block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader became, at 0.7.0, the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/era5_loader.esm, referenced as subsystem `pl`; at esm 1.0.0 it is the `ERA5_pl` entry in THIS file's `data_sources` and the standalone file is gone.\n\nUpstream constructor ERA5(domaininfo; name=:ERA5, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) created an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon (rad), lat (rad), lev (dimensionless, 1–37 integer index), t_ref (s)\n  - Sub-system 'pl' containing one observed equation per NetCDF variable (16 variables): pl₊t, pl₊u, pl₊v, pl₊w, pl₊q, pl₊r, pl₊z, pl₊d, pl₊vo, pl₊o3, pl₊cc, pl₊ciwc, pl₊clwc, pl₊crwc, pl₊cswc, pl₊pv. These are now provided directly by the loader subsystem `pl` (ERA5.pl.<var>), not by per-variable interp_unsafe observed equations.\n  - Top-level observed variables: P(t) ~ hPa2Pa * era5_P_itp(lev) where hPa2Pa=100.0; δxδlon(t) ~ lon2m * cos(lat) [lat/lon domains only]; δyδlat(t) ~ lat2meters [lat/lon domains only].\n  - couple2 with MeanWindCoupler: MeanWind.v_lon ~ ERA5.pl.u, MeanWind.v_lat ~ ERA5.pl.v, MeanWind.v_lev ~ ERA5.pl.w.\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): ERA5's native grid.crs.projection is 'longlat' (geographic WGS84), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1) — the IDENTITY transform (a no-op for an unprojected grid). No reprojection parameters are needed.\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. ERA5 is stored on a regular non-staggered grid, but per the migration spec the horizontal wind components u and v are regridded by B-spline interpolation (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3) and every centered scalar — temperature, humidity, geopotential, cloud water species, ozone, divergence/vorticity, and the vertical-velocity field w (omega, a centered scalar, not a horizontal wind) — by conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm).\n\ngt-6ohw gap — δPδlev omitted:\n  Upstream source (era5.jl:454,516) computes δPδlev(t) ~ hPa2Pa * DataInterpolations.derivative(era5_P_itp, lev). This requires calling the derivative of a LinearInterpolation object with respect to its argument (lev); the ESM expression language does not support DataInterpolations.derivative get_unit (gap gt-6ohw). δPδlev is therefore omitted from this migration. When gt-6ohw is resolved, add a δPδlev observed = 100.0 * derivative(era5_pressure_levels_pa, lev).\n\nCoordinate conventions:\n  - lev: 1-based integer index into ERA5_PRESSURE_LEVELS_HPA, increasing upward (1 = 1000 hPa near-surface, 37 = 1 hPa top-of-atmosphere). Fractional values interpolate between levels.\n  - lon/lat: radians; the runtime regridder converts to degrees for spatial interpolation against the 0.25°×0.25° ERA5 grid.\n  - t_ref: seconds since the Julian date epoch, set from DomainInfo.get_tref(domaininfo) at construction time.\n  - δxδlon and δyδlat: emitted only for lat/lon coordinate domains, not for projected (x/y) domains."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. The runtime regridder converts radians to degrees for spatial interpolation against the ERA5 0.25°×0.25° grid."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. The runtime regridder converts radians to degrees for spatial interpolation against the ERA5 0.25°×0.25° grid."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "ERA5 pressure level index (dimensionless, 1-based). Index 1 corresponds to the near-surface level (1000 hPa); index 37 corresponds to the top-of-atmosphere level (1 hPa). Fractional values interpolate linearly between adjacent pressure levels. Coupled from the simulation domain's lev coordinate."
        },
        "t_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Reference epoch (seconds since the Julian date epoch) from which the ERA5 file time axis (valid_time) is offset. Set from DomainInfo.get_tref(domaininfo) at construction time."
        },
        "t_interp_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2): simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the interpolated loader — i.e. a time at which a fresh ERA5 record lands, so the interpolation weight is 0 there. Together with dt_interp it lets the model locate the current time within its bracketing pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps (the provider still LOADS the two bracketing records; this fixes only the phase of the weight). Set once by the runner (like the src-geometry params); for a run whose t=0 coincides with an ERA5 hour, 0.0 is correct."
        },
        "dt_interp": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 3600.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the loader's cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — ERA5 is hourly, so 3600. Set by the runner to match the loader frequency. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so the model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider loaded."
        },
        "w_time": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1): the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of ERA5 records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref)/dt_interp) = u - floor(u). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0→1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer that blends the two bracketing fields as (1 - w_time)*F0 + w_time*F1 gets a value that varies smoothly in time between the hourly ERA5 records (replacing the former piecewise-constant hourly step). It stays consistent with WHICH two records the provider loaded because both floor the same cadence grid (t_interp_ref phase, dt_interp step). At the end of the data the provider returns a degenerate bracket (both records equal), so any w yields the held endpoint. Consumers: wildlandfire Era5Regrid conservatively regrids BOTH bracket records at the (discrete) hourly cadence and blends the two fire-grid fields with w_time (regrid-then-blend == blend-then-regrid, conservative regrid being linear), so only this cheap blend is per-step; a pointwise consumer blends the two record values directly."
        },
        "P": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Atmospheric pressure at the current level index (Pa). P = hPa2Pa * era5_P_itp(lev) = 100.0 * LinearInterpolation(ERA5_PRESSURE_LEVELS_HPA, 1:37)(lev). Computed from the era5_pressure_levels_pa function table (37 entries, Pa). For integer lev this returns exact ERA5 standard pressure levels; for fractional lev it linearly interpolates between adjacent levels."
        },
        "δxδlon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: x-distance per unit longitude (m rad⁻¹). δxδlon = lon2m·cos(lat) where lon2m = 40075×10³/(2π) ≈ 6378134.3 m rad⁻¹ (equatorial circumference metric). Emitted only in lat/lon coordinate domains; the upstream ERA5 constructor includes this equation only when :lat is in DomainInfo.pvars."
        },
        "δyδlat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: y-distance per unit latitude (m rad⁻¹). δyδlat = lat2meters = 111.32×10³·(180/π) ≈ 6378166.0 m rad⁻¹. Constant (does not depend on position). Emitted only in lat/lon coordinate domains; the upstream ERA5 constructor includes this equation only when :lat is in DomainInfo.pvars."
        },
        "t": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Temperature (K). ERA5 NetCDF short name 't'.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "ERA5_pl",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "t",
              "description": "Temperature (K). ERA5 NetCDF short name 't'."
            }
          }
        },
        "u": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "U component of wind — zonal wind (m/s). ERA5 NetCDF short name 'u'.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "ERA5_pl",
